    "result_text": "All tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature end-to-end, following the existing PetClinic conventions for derived owner fields.\n\n**What the change does:** the create/update request may now include an optional `title` (`MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`), and the owner's read-only `salutation` is returned as `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is supplied.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` as an optional input to `OwnerFields` (an enum for MR/MRS/MS/DR, giving free 400 validation on bad values) and `salutation` as a read-only derived field on `Owner`. The DTOs regenerate from this at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` column with getter/setter, so the value persists.\n\n3. **`Salutation.java`** (new model class) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility unit with a `forOwner(owner)` static factory that composes the salutation. This mirrors the existing derived-field classes like `ContactPreference` and `AgeBand`.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` line delegating `salutation` to `Salutation.forOwner(...)`, alongside the other derived mappings. MapStruct auto-bridges the generated `TitleEnum` \u2194 the entity's `String title`.\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.updateOwner`** \u2014 copies `title` alongside the other editable fields for consistency.\n\n6. **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `title` column.\n\nThe logic stays where it belongs: composition in the `Salutation` model, wiring in the mapper, persistence in the entity/schema \u2014 nothing accumulated into a catch-all. The acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` and the full suite pass.",
